q('M','Core Web Vitals','LCP meaning','Which metric tracks when the largest eligible content element becomes visible in the viewport during loading?','Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)','LCP concerns perceived loading of major content. INP measures responsiveness, and CLS measures unexpected layout instability.','Match the metric to loading.','Which event represents the main content appearing?','web:lcp',wrong=['Interaction to Next Paint (INP)','Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)','Total JavaScript file count'])
q('C','Core Web Vitals','INP meaning','What does INP reveal that measuring only network load time misses?','It measures responsiveness across page interactions. It includes delay before handling, handler work and delay until the next paint for the measured interaction. Slow interaction feedback can occur even after a page has loaded quickly.','A short event callback does not guarantee low INP if input waits behind long tasks. Network speed is only one part of user experience.','Follow interaction to visible response.','What happens before and after the handler itself?','web:inp')
q('B','Core Web Vitals','Image space and CLS','Why can this image shift text below it during loading, and what should be added?','Its aspect ratio is not reserved. Add correct width and height attributes or an equivalent CSS aspect-ratio with a responsive size.','Before the image dimensions are known, insufficient space may be reserved.~Loading reveals its dimensions and moves following content.~Reserving the correct ratio stabilizes layout while allowing responsive sizing.','Reserve geometry early.','Does the browser know the aspect ratio?','web:optimize-cls','<img src="/banner.jpg" alt="Team at the conference">\n<p>Conference details</p>')
q('W','Accessibility','Icon button name','Write an icon-only close button with an accessible name. Treat the icon as decorative.','<button type="button" aria-label="Close dialog">\n  <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24">\n    <path d="M6 6L18 18M18 6L6 18" stroke="currentColor" />\n  </svg>\n</button>','The native button provides keyboard activation.~aria-label names its action.~The decorative SVG is hidden from the accessibility tree so it does not add redundant naming. Wire the actual close behavior separately.','Name the action, not the icon shape.','Should the SVG announce separate content?','wai:button/','<!-- Write the semantic close control. -->')
q('M','Accessibility','Decorative images','What alt value is appropriate for an image that adds no information beyond adjacent content?','alt=""','An empty alt marks a purely decorative image for assistive technology. Omitting alt can cause an unhelpful filename announcement; a generic word adds noise.','Avoid repeating information.','Should this image have an accessible name?','https://www.w3.org/WAI/tutorials/images/decorative/',wrong=['Omit alt entirely.','alt="image"','alt set to the filename.'])
q('C','SEO','Document title','Why should each meaningful page have a descriptive document title?','It identifies the page in browser tabs and assistive navigation. It also provides useful information to search systems. Keep it accurate and specific rather than repeating a generic brand-only title everywhere.','A title is not a guarantee of a particular search-result presentation. It remains important for users even when search systems choose different display text.','A page needs an identity outside its body.','Can users distinguish several open tabs?','mdn:Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/title')
q('S','Loading','LCP lazy loading','Should the likely above-the-fold LCP image normally use loading="lazy"?','Usually no, because delaying its discovery or fetch can worsen LCP. Load the critical image promptly and consider appropriate priority hints. Reserve lazy loading for images that can wait.','Lazy loading reduces unnecessary work but can hurt when applied to the most important initial content. Measure the actual LCP element rather than assuming every hero is it.','Optimize the critical resource’s arrival.','Is this content needed for the initial view?','web:optimize-lcp')
q('W','Loading','Below-fold image','Write a responsive below-fold image with native lazy loading, known dimensions 800 by 600, and meaningful alt text.','<img src="/workshop.jpg" alt="Participants building a wooden chair"\n  width="800" height="600" loading="lazy"\n  style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;">','Known dimensions reserve a 4:3 ratio.~Lazy loading allows the browser to defer offscreen fetch work.~Responsive styling scales the image without distorting its ratio. Do not apply this policy blindly to critical above-fold imagery.','Combine loading policy with stable dimensions.','Which attributes reserve the ratio?','mdn:Web/Performance/Guides/Lazy_loading#images_and_iframes','<!-- The image is below the initial viewport. Write the img element. -->')
q('C','Bundles','Code splitting','How does route or feature code splitting improve initial loading, and what tradeoff does it introduce?','It defers code not needed for the initial view. This reduces initial download and execution work. Later navigation may need extra requests, so use loading UI and sensible prefetching.','Splitting every tiny function creates overhead and does not eliminate total work. The boundary should follow meaningful user journeys and dependency size.','Move work to when it is needed.','What latency can appear on first use?','web:reduce-javascript-payloads-with-code-splitting')
q('S','Bundles','Bundle analysis','A production bundle grows after adding a chart package. What evidence should guide the fix?','Inspect the built bundle and its dependency graph. Identify which modules entered the initial route and why. Consider a smaller import surface, deferred loading or a different dependency, then compare production results.','Package size on a registry is not the same as shipped route cost. Tree shaking, duplicated versions and client boundaries affect the final output.','Measure shipped code.','Which import pulled the package into the initial path?','next:app/guides/package-bundling')
q('B','Rendering','Layout thrashing','What makes this loop expensive, and how should reads and writes be reorganized?','It interleaves layout-affecting writes with geometry reads. Read required geometry first, compute results, then batch writes where the intended behavior permits.','Each height write can invalidate layout.~The next offsetHeight read can force synchronous layout.~Batching avoids repeated invalidation/measurement cycles; preserve semantics if measurements intentionally depend on previous writes.','Track invalidation before each read.','Can measurements be collected before mutations?','web:avoid-large-complex-layouts-and-layout-thrashing','for (const element of elements) {\n  element.style.height = `${element.offsetHeight + 1}px`;\n}')
q('M','Keyboard','Native button activation','Which keys activate a focused native button in standard keyboard interaction?','Enter and Space.','Native buttons implement standard keyboard behavior. A clickable div does not gain those semantics merely from styling or a click handler.','Use the expected control pattern.','How do keyboard users activate a button?','wai:button/',wrong=['Only Escape.','Only the arrow keys.','Only Tab.'])
q('S','Accessibility','Modal focus lifecycle','What focus behavior should a modal dialog implement when opening and closing?','Move focus to an appropriate element inside on open. Keep keyboard navigation within the active modal. Restore focus to the invoking control or a logical successor on close.','Visual dimming alone does not constrain keyboard access. Initial focus should consider content structure and destructive actions rather than always choosing the first button blindly.','Follow the user’s entry and exit points.','Where should focus return?','wai:dialog-modal/')
q('W','Accessibility','Skip link','Write a skip link targeting the main content region, making the target programmatically focusable.','<a href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>\n<nav aria-label="Primary">Navigation links</nav>\n<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">\n  <h1>Account overview</h1>\n</main>','The first link targets the main region.~tabindex=-1 permits programmatic focus without adding another normal tab stop.~Ensure the skip link becomes visibly usable on focus if it is visually hidden by CSS.','Bypass repeated navigation.','The destination needs a stable ID.','https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/bypass-blocks.html','<!-- Write a minimal skip-link and main-content structure. -->')
q('C','WCAG','Text contrast','For ordinary text under WCAG AA, what contrast target should be checked, and why is color alone insufficient for errors?','Ordinary text generally needs a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1. Large text has a 3:1 threshold under the defined criteria. Errors should also have text or another noncolor indication so meaning is not conveyed only by hue.','Contrast and use-of-color requirements address different barriers. Disabled controls and purely decorative content have specific exceptions, so apply the criterion to the actual content.','Distinguish readability from meaning.','Would the error still be understood without color?','https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/contrast-minimum.html')
q('W','SEO','Meta description','Write a head fragment with a descriptive title and meta description for an invoice dashboard.','<title>Invoices | Acme Workspace</title>\n<meta name="description" content="Review invoices, track payment status, and manage billing in Acme Workspace.">','The title identifies the page.~The description summarizes its purpose.~Search systems may choose other snippets; metadata should describe actual visible content rather than promise unsupported features.','Use standard metadata elements.','Which attribute names the description field?','mdn:Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/meta/name','<!-- Write the head metadata fragment. -->')
q('S','Structured data','JSON-LD accuracy','When adding JSON-LD to a product page, what makes the structured data trustworthy and safe to embed?','It should describe the actual visible product and current facts. Serialize data and escape unsafe HTML-significant content before embedding it in a script. Validate the vocabulary and avoid claims the page does not support.','Valid JSON alone does not guarantee safe HTML embedding or accurate structured data. JSON-LD is a machine-readable description, not a shortcut to guaranteed rich results.','Separate semantic accuracy from embedding safety.','Could a value contain a closing script sequence?','next:app/guides/json-ld')
q('A','SEO','SSR and CSR tradeoffs','How should SSR versus CSR be evaluated for a public content page’s discoverability?','Server-rendered HTML exposes meaningful initial content without waiting for client execution. CSR can still be processed by capable crawlers but adds rendering dependencies and delays. Preserve semantic content, valid links and metadata whichever rendering model is chosen.','SSR alone does not guarantee indexing or good rankings. Authentication, robots rules, canonicalization and content quality remain separate concerns.','Compare what arrives in the first response.','Does meaningful content require client execution?','web:rendering-on-the-web')
q('S','Memory','Leak investigation','A page becomes slower after repeatedly opening and closing a panel. What memory evidence should you collect?','Repeat the same interaction and compare heap snapshots after cleanup opportunities. Inspect retained detached DOM nodes and their retaining paths. Look for listeners, timers, observers or caches that keep disposed resources reachable.','A temporary allocation spike is not necessarily a leak. The useful signal is persistent growth tied to resources that should have been released.','Find what remains reachable.','Which owner retains a supposedly disposed node?','https://developer.chrome.com/docs/devtools/memory-problems')
q('C','Metrics','Field and lab measurements','Why can good local Lighthouse results coexist with poor field Core Web Vitals?','Lab tests run under a controlled scenario. Field data reflects real devices, networks and user interactions across visits. Compare like-for-like conditions and investigate the actual field distribution.','One fast local run does not represent all users. Some interaction and long-session layout problems may not occur during a short synthetic test.','Population and scenario differ.','What user behavior does the lab run omit?','web:lab-and-field-data-differences')
q('M','Core Web Vitals','Good thresholds','Which set gives the good Core Web Vitals thresholds assessed at the 75th percentile?','LCP ≤ 2.5 s, INP ≤ 200 ms, CLS ≤ 0.1.','The thresholds cover loading, responsiveness and stability. Averages can hide poor experiences, so the percentile criterion matters.','Match each metric’s unit.','CLS is unitless, unlike time metrics.','web:vitals',wrong=['LCP ≤ 10 s, INP ≤ 1 s, CLS ≤ 1.0.','LCP ≤ 200 ms, INP ≤ 2.5 s, CLS ≤ 10.','All three must equal zero on every visit.'])
q('S','Main thread','Long task reduction','A click handler performs 300 ms of CPU work before updating the screen. What changes can reduce interaction latency?','Reduce unnecessary computation first. Move suitable heavy computation to a worker or split it into yielding tasks. Provide prompt feedback and measure the resulting interaction rather than only total throughput.','A microtask loop does not necessarily yield to rendering. Deferring all work without considering feedback can merely move the same visible delay.','The main thread cannot paint while occupied.','Where can work yield or run elsewhere?','web:optimize-long-tasks')
q('B','Accessibility','ARIA without behavior','Why is this custom control not an accessible replacement for a button, and what is the simplest correction?','role alone does not add focus or keyboard behavior. Replace it with: <button type="button" onclick="save()">Save</button>.','The div exposes a role but is not natively keyboard-focusable.~It lacks standard Enter/Space activation.~A native button supplies those behaviors; styling can preserve the desired appearance.','Semantics do not implement interaction.','Can a keyboard user reach and activate it?','wai:button/','<div role="button" onclick="save()">Save</div>')
q('A','Accessibility','Roving tabindex','For a composite toolbar, how does roving tabindex reduce tab stops while retaining keyboard access?','Give one current item tabindex=0 and the others tabindex=-1. Use the pattern’s arrow-key behavior to move focus and update that current item. Tab enters or leaves the composite instead of visiting every control.','The keyboard pattern must match the widget role and orientation. Simply setting all items to -1 makes the toolbar unreachable.','Separate entry into the widget from movement within it.','Which item is the single tab stop?','wai:toolbar/')
q('U','Core Web Vitals','CLS after initial load','Follow-up to PAS-003: why should CLS testing continue after the first screen appears?','Unexpected shifts can occur during later interactions and loading. Ads, fonts and dynamically inserted content can move existing elements. Measure representative page lifetimes and distinguish expected interaction-related exclusions from unrelated shifts.','A stable initial screenshot does not prove long-session stability. CLS uses defined session-window and recent-input rules, not a simple count of all movement.','Layout changes continue after load.','Which late content can displace existing UI?','web:cls')
