q('B','Data bugs','Zero index truthiness','Removing the first item fails, while missing items can remove the last one. Correct this condition.','Index 0 is falsy and -1 is truthy. Use: if (index !== -1) items.splice(index, 1);','findIndex returns 0 for the first match and -1 for absence.~The truthiness test reverses those two intended cases.~Compare the documented sentinel explicitly; splice(-1, 1) targets the last entry.','An index is not a boolean.','Which exact number means not found?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/findIndex','const index = items.findIndex(item => item.id === id);\nif (index) items.splice(index, 1);')
q('F','Storage bugs','Malformed persisted JSON','Write readPreferences() that returns parsed object preferences from localStorage or {} for missing, malformed, nonobject or inaccessible storage. Reject arrays and null.','function readPreferences() {\n  try {\n    const raw = localStorage.getItem("preferences");\n    if (raw === null) return {};\n    const value = JSON.parse(raw);\n    return value !== null && typeof value === "object"\n      && !Array.isArray(value) ? value : {};\n  } catch {\n    return {};\n  }\n}','Read storage inside the guarded region because access can fail.~Parse only a present string and validate the container shape.~Fallback handles corrupt data without crashing startup; individual preference fields still need domain validation.','Stored data can outlive application versions.','Guard both storage access and parsing.','mdn:Web/API/Window/localStorage','// Existing startup code crashes on corrupt data:\nconst preferences = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("preferences"));')
q('S','CSS bugs','Percentage height','A child with height: 100% remains content-sized because its parent has auto height. What is the missing layout assumption?','Percentage height needs an appropriate definite containing-block height in this situation. Give the parent a defined height or use a layout mechanism suited to filling available space. Avoid assuming 100% always means viewport height.','Percentages resolve against a containing block, not an intuitive visual region. Flex and grid have additional sizing rules, so inspect the actual formatting context.','Find the percentage reference size.','Is the parent’s height definite?','mdn:Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/height','.parent { height: auto; }\n.child { height: 100%; }')
q('M','Forms bugs','Disabled submission loss','A disabled account-number input is absent from FormData. Which change preserves a visible noneditable text value in normal form submission?','Use readonly instead of disabled on the text input.','Disabled controls are not successful submitted controls. Readonly text inputs remain submitted when named; server validation must still distrust the submitted value.','Noneditable does not have to mean disabled.','Which state excludes a control from submission?','mdn:Web/HTML/Reference/Attributes/disabled','<input name="account" value="A-42" disabled>',wrong=['Add aria-label while keeping disabled.','Increase the input z-index.','Remove name and keep disabled.'])
q('B','React bugs','Object as child','Why does this component throw, and what JSX displays the user’s name?','A plain object is not a renderable React child. Use: return <p>{user.name}</p>;','The expression supplies the entire user object as a child.~React cannot render that object directly.~Select renderable fields or explicitly serialize for a diagnostic view.','JSX expressions still have value types.','Which field is the intended visible text?','react:learn/javascript-in-jsx-with-curly-braces#where-to-use-curly-braces','function UserLabel({ user }) {\n  return <p>{user}</p>;\n}')
q('B','Fetch bugs','Consumed response body','Why does the second body read reject, and what should be changed when both logging and returning JSON are needed?','Response bodies are consumable once. Parse once, log that parsed value, and return the same value; clone before reading only if two independent body reads are truly needed.','The first json call consumes the body stream.~The second read encounters an already-used body.~Reusing parsed data avoids another decode and unnecessary buffering.','A response body is a stream.','Can one stream be consumed twice?','mdn:Web/API/Fetch_API/Using_Fetch#locked_and_disturbed_streams','const response = await fetch("/api/data");\nconsole.log(await response.json());\nreturn response.json();')
q('S','Forms bugs','Numeric input empty state','A controlled number input stores Number(event.target.value), so clearing it immediately displays zero. How should empty editing state be modeled?','Keep the editable value as text or explicitly model an empty state. Convert and validate at a suitable boundary such as submission. Do not force every intermediate edit into a valid number.','Number("") equals zero, so the conversion erases the distinction. Inputs can have temporary states that are not yet valid domain values.','Editing state differs from submitted data.','Is an empty field intended to mean zero?','react:reference/react-dom/components/input','onChange={event => setAmount(Number(event.target.value))}')
q('B','Cancellation bugs','Reused AbortController','Why does the second request reject immediately, and how should controllers be scoped?','An aborted signal stays aborted. Create a new AbortController for each new independently cancelable request lifecycle.','The first abort permanently marks the signal.~The later fetch receives that already-aborted signal.~A controller is not resettable; reuse only when intentionally canceling one shared group.','Abort is a one-way state change.','Was this signal already canceled?','mdn:Web/API/AbortSignal#examples','const controller = new AbortController();\ncontroller.abort();\nfetch("/api/new-search", { signal: controller.signal });')
q('S','Rate limiting bugs','Debouncer recreation','Search calls are not coalesced because a new debounce wrapper is created inside every input event. What should change?','Create one wrapper for the intended input lifecycle. Reuse it across the burst of events. Cancel its pending work when that lifecycle ends.','Each wrapper has its own timer state. Independent wrappers cannot cancel each other’s pending callbacks, so the delay occurs without debouncing the burst.','The timer state belongs to the wrapper.','How many independent timers are created?','mdn:Glossary/Debounce','input.addEventListener("input", event => {\n  const delayedSearch = debounce(search, 300);\n  delayedSearch(event.target.value);\n});')
q('F','React races','Obsolete async response','Write UserName({ id, loadUser }) that ignores an obsolete request result after id changes or unmount. loadUser(id) returns Promise<{name:string}> and has stable identity.','import { useEffect, useState } from "react";\n\nexport default function UserName({ id, loadUser }) {\n  const [result, setResult] = useState({ id, name: "", error: "" });\n  useEffect(() => {\n    let active = true;\n    loadUser(id).then(\n      user => { if (active) setResult({ id, name: user.name, error: "" }); },\n      () => { if (active) setResult({ id, name: "", error: "Unable to load" }); }\n    );\n    return () => { active = false; };\n  }, [id, loadUser]);\n  if (result.id !== id) return <p>Loading</p>;\n  if (result.error) return <p role="alert">{result.error}</p>;\n  return <p>{result.name || "Loading"}</p>;\n}\n','Each Effect instance owns an active flag.~Cleanup invalidates its callbacks before a replacement Effect starts.~Results are also keyed by id so old data is not shown for a new id. This suppresses obsolete commits but does not cancel network work.','Each request needs a relevance check.','Can cleanup invalidate the old callback?','react:reference/react/useEffect#fetching-data-with-effects','// A naive implementation commits every loadUser(id) result.\n// Replace it with a complete component that ignores obsolete results.')
q('B','External store bugs','Mutated snapshot identity','Why can useSyncExternalStore consumers miss this update, and what should the store change?','getSnapshot returns the same mutated object. Replace snapshot with a new immutable object before notifying: snapshot = { ...snapshot, count: snapshot.count + 1 };','The store edits the current object in place.~Consumers compare snapshot identity and may see no change.~A new object for changed data and stable identity for unchanged data satisfy the snapshot contract.','Identity signals version changes.','Was a new snapshot produced?','react:reference/react/useSyncExternalStore#parameters','const snapshot = { count: 0 };\nfunction increment() {\n  snapshot.count++;\n  listeners.forEach(listener => listener());\n}\nconst getSnapshot = () => snapshot;')
q('P','URL bugs','Duplicate query keys','What does this filter parser log?','red\nred,blue','get returns the first value for the key.~getAll returns every value in order.~Choosing get for a multi-select filter silently drops later selections.','Repeated keys are valid.','Which method preserves all selections?','mdn:Web/API/URLSearchParams/getAll','const params = new URLSearchParams("tag=red&tag=blue");\nconsole.log(params.get("tag"));\nconsole.log(params.getAll("tag").join(","));')
q('T','Error bugs','Finally overrides failure','What does this function log, and use the output to explain why the failure disappears?','ok','try throws an Error.~finally executes and returns ok.~That return replaces the pending throw, so the caller sees success. Avoid control-flow returns in cleanup unless overriding the outcome is intentional.','finally can replace the pending completion.','Which return happens last?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/try...catch#returning_from_a_finally_block','function save() {\n  try {\n    throw new Error("failed");\n  } finally {\n    return "ok";\n  }\n}\nconsole.log(save());')
q('S','Keyboard bugs','Visual order mismatch','A form uses flex-direction: row-reverse, but Tab moves in the original DOM order. How should the mismatch be resolved?','Keep a logical DOM order that matches the intended reading and navigation sequence. Adjust layout without creating a confusing visual order. Avoid positive tabindex values as a patch for structural order problems.','CSS visual reordering does not generally reorder sequential keyboard navigation. Screen-reader reading order also follows document semantics rather than visual placement.','Compare DOM order with screen order.','Should CSS be changing meaningful sequence?','mdn:Web/CSS/Guides/Flexible_box_layout/Ordering_items','.actions {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: row-reverse;\n}')
q('S','Deployment bugs','Build-time public configuration','The same Next.js build is promoted to production, but its NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL still points to staging. Why, and what deployment policy fixes it?','Public variables are inlined during the build. Changing only the runtime environment does not rewrite that bundle. Rebuild for the target environment or implement a deliberate runtime public-configuration mechanism.','The browser receives JavaScript containing the earlier value. This differs from server-only variables read at request time.','Find when the value was embedded.','Was the bundle rebuilt after changing the variable?','next:app/guides/environment-variables#bundling-environment-variables-for-the-browser')
q('B','Caching bugs','Missing tenant cache key','A shared Map caches reports by reportId, but IDs repeat across tenants. Identify the bug and a safe key shape.','The key omits tenant identity. Use a collision-safe composite such as JSON.stringify([tenantId, reportId]) and enforce authorization before access.','Tenant A populates a reportId entry.~Tenant B can hit that same entry despite different data ownership.~Include every identity dimension and avoid delimiter-based collisions. A correct key does not replace permission checks.','The result depends on more than one ID.','Could two tenants use the same reportId?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Map','const key = reportId;\nif (cache.has(key)) return cache.get(key);\nconst report = await loadReport(tenantId, reportId);\ncache.set(key, report);\nreturn report;')
q('B','Worker bugs','Detached typed-array storage','Why can the sender no longer reuse this typed array’s bytes after sending it, and what should change if both sides need data?','Transferring its buffer detaches the sender’s storage. Omit the transfer list to clone, or transfer a deliberately copied buffer instead.','The transfer list moves the underlying ArrayBuffer.~The sender’s view no longer has usable original storage.~Choose copying when both contexts must retain independent data; transferring is appropriate for ownership handoff.','The view depends on its buffer.','Was ownership copied or moved?','mdn:Web/API/Web_Workers_API/Transferable_objects','const bytes = new Uint8Array([1, 2, 3]);\nworker.postMessage(bytes, [bytes.buffer]);\n// Later sender code expects to read the original bytes.')
q('S','Hydration bugs','Invalid interactive nesting','Server-rendered nested buttons trigger hydration warnings. Why should the markup be fixed instead of suppressing the warning?','Nested interactive button content is invalid HTML. Browser parsing can produce a tree different from the JSX expectation. Use separate valid controls or restructure the outer container so server and client agree.','Hydration compares against the parsed browser DOM, not the original source string. A warning flag does not restore valid interaction semantics.','The HTML parser may repair invalid structure.','Are interactive controls allowed inside this button?','next:messages/react-hydration-error','<button>\n  Open card\n  <button>Delete</button>\n</button>')
q('A','Optimistic bugs','Temporary identifier reconciliation','An optimistic new row has a temporary ID, then the server returns a permanent ID. How should the app avoid duplicates and lost pending state?','Track the mutation with a stable client correlation ID. Reconcile the confirmed record with its optimistic counterpart using that correlation. Decide deliberately whether UI identity should remain stable or reset after confirmation.','Appending the server row without reconciliation duplicates the record. Using only a server ID that does not yet exist cannot identify the pending operation.','Connect the request to its provisional row.','Which identifier survives the round trip?','react:reference/react/useOptimistic')
q('U','Accessibility bugs','Hidden menu focus','Follow-up to DBG-014: a visually hidden menu remains reachable by Tab because it only has opacity: 0. What should its closed-state contract include?','Remove closed content from interaction with an appropriate hidden or inert strategy. Keep focus outside the closed menu and restore it logically when closing. Synchronize expanded-state semantics with the actual interaction state.','Opacity only changes appearance. It does not inherently remove focusability or accessibility-tree exposure, so invisible controls can still trap or confuse users.','Visibility and interactivity are separate.','Can an invisible item still receive focus?','mdn:Web/HTML/Reference/Global_attributes/inert')
